WEBVTT

00:00:01.50 --> 00:00:06.98
This is journey fifteen of Hewn, the software factory: browse the design system.

00:00:06.98 --> 00:00:12.81
Stage three extracts a design system from the exported mocks, with tokens for colour,

00:00:12.81 --> 00:00:18.01
type, spacing, radius, elevation and motion, and a page for every component.

00:00:18.01 --> 00:00:23.15
Owners and Viewers want to look through it without leaving Mission Control,

00:00:23.15 --> 00:00:24.59
in light and in dark.

00:00:24.59 --> 00:00:29.39
This video walks through how it was built: the design system endpoint,

00:00:29.39 --> 00:00:34.73
the token pages stage three now writes, the tab that reuses journey fourteen's

00:00:34.73 --> 00:00:36.99
sandboxed preview, and the tests.

00:00:38.14 --> 00:00:44.13
A user opens a project's Design system and sees its token pages under Foundations

00:00:44.13 --> 00:00:47.16
and its component pages under Components.

00:00:47.16 --> 00:00:51.81
Choosing one opens it in the same sandboxed preview as Designs,

00:00:51.81 --> 00:00:56.98
served from the separate preview origin, at any width from X S to X L,

00:00:56.98 --> 00:00:58.24
in light or dark.

00:00:59.39 --> 00:01:00.58
Here is the flow.

00:01:00.58 --> 00:01:03.58
The tab asks the API for the design system.

00:01:03.58 --> 00:01:08.05
The API reads tokens dot json at the head of the default branch,

00:01:08.05 --> 00:01:11.96
lists the token and component pages at that same commit,

00:01:11.96 --> 00:01:14.33
and signs one preview link for it.

00:01:14.33 --> 00:01:19.99
The frame then loads each page from the preview host that journey fourteen built,

00:01:19.99 --> 00:01:21.38
in the same sandbox.

00:01:22.53 --> 00:01:25.13
The new pieces sit beside the old ones.

00:01:25.13 --> 00:01:30.80
A design system component and a design system handler are new; the sandboxed preview,

00:01:30.80 --> 00:01:34.87
the preview tokens and the preview host are reused unchanged,

00:01:34.87 --> 00:01:40.41
and the width and theme controls moved into a small component that both tabs share.

00:01:41.56 --> 00:01:45.44
Stage three writes no manifest, so the folders are the list.

00:01:45.44 --> 00:01:49.97
A project has a design system once tokens dot json exists at the head.

00:01:49.97 --> 00:01:55.28
The handler reads it, then lists the files under foundations and components at the

00:01:55.28 --> 00:02:00.13
commit it was read at, so one signed token covers every page and its links.

00:02:00.13 --> 00:02:04.27
If the tokens can't be parsed, or GitHub can't list the folders,

00:02:04.27 --> 00:02:07.50
the answer is a five oh two that names the commit.

00:02:07.85 --> 00:02:12.05
Token pages come in the order of the token groups, colour first,

00:02:12.05 --> 00:02:14.28
each with its group's token count.

00:02:14.28 --> 00:02:19.59
Colour has light and dark values, so it counts one theme and says light and dark.

00:02:20.74 --> 00:02:23.93
The token pages come from stage three itself.

00:02:23.93 --> 00:02:28.40
Its task now asks for a page per token group under foundations,

00:02:28.40 --> 00:02:33.09
following the html element's data theme attribute as the mocks do.

00:02:33.09 --> 00:02:39.12
The scripted agent the tests and videos use writes them from the tokens it extracted,

00:02:39.12 --> 00:02:42.18
with the dark values under data theme dark.

00:02:43.33 --> 00:02:48.00
In Mission Control, the tab shows the page's title with its token count,

00:02:48.00 --> 00:02:53.19
the shared width and theme controls, and the same sandboxed preview component as

00:02:53.19 --> 00:02:53.71
Designs.

00:02:53.71 --> 00:02:59.10
The caption says it was served from the preview origin in the same sandboxed frame,

00:02:59.10 --> 00:03:01.37
at what width, and from which path.

00:03:02.52 --> 00:03:07.08
Here is what the preview host answers for the colour page in dark.

00:03:07.08 --> 00:03:12.81
A sandbox content security policy, no sniffing, no referrer, a short private cache,

00:03:12.81 --> 00:03:14.26
and no cookie at all.

00:03:14.26 --> 00:03:18.05
The page runs in an opaque origin on another host name,

00:03:18.05 --> 00:03:21.85
so it can't reach Mission Control's cookies or storage.

00:03:23.00 --> 00:03:28.14
The backend tests came first, and failed with not found: there was no route.

00:03:28.14 --> 00:03:32.80
Six tests now cover the listing in the token order, the token counts,

00:03:32.80 --> 00:03:37.40
both kinds of page opening in the same sandbox with their own links,

00:03:37.40 --> 00:03:41.52
a project before stage three, unreadable tokens, and Viewers.

00:03:41.87 --> 00:03:47.45
End to end, a test checks the frame's source is on the preview origin and sandboxed,

00:03:47.45 --> 00:03:52.83
reads the theme and background inside the real frame as it switches from light to

00:03:52.83 --> 00:03:57.42
dark, then opens a component page that keeps the theme and the width.

00:03:57.77 --> 00:04:01.75
All green, the backend has two hundred and twenty eight tests,

00:04:01.75 --> 00:04:06.62
the worker one hundred and forty four, and the frontend four new view tests.

00:04:06.62 --> 00:04:10.41
End to end, there are twelve new tests: four for behaviour,

00:04:10.41 --> 00:04:14.90
four visual comparisons with the mocks, and four accessibility checks.

00:04:16.05 --> 00:04:20.89
Here is Kiln Booking, after a real worker ran stages zero to three.

00:04:20.89 --> 00:04:25.15
Its Design system tab lists six token pages and the button.

00:04:25.15 --> 00:04:30.49
Typography, spacing, then colour, in dark, then the button, back to light,

00:04:30.49 --> 00:04:31.65
and phone width.

00:04:32.00 --> 00:04:37.31
The colour tokens in light, then in dark, where every swatch takes its dark value

00:04:37.31 --> 00:04:38.36
from the tokens.

00:04:38.36 --> 00:04:43.47
The button in dark, then in light, with the accent colour following the theme.

00:04:43.82 --> 00:04:48.02
The tab works in Mission Control's dark mode and on a phone.

00:04:48.02 --> 00:04:52.35
A project before stage three says it has no design system yet,

00:04:52.35 --> 00:04:56.41
while unreadable tokens name their commit, with try again.

00:04:57.56 --> 00:04:59.54
Journey fifteen is complete.

00:04:59.54 --> 00:05:05.33
The design system tab lists token and component pages from the folders stage three

00:05:05.33 --> 00:05:08.58
wrote, with token counts from tokens dot json.

00:05:08.58 --> 00:05:13.25
Every page opens in the same signed, sandboxed preview as Designs,

00:05:13.25 --> 00:05:14.52
on its own origin.

00:05:14.52 --> 00:05:19.61
And light and dark, and every width, work just as they do for the mocks.

00:05:19.61 --> 00:05:21.52
Next comes journey sixteen.
